  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Uveitis through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone is associated with Iritis, which in turn is linked to Fluorometholone and subsequently to Uveitis. Similarly, Hydrocortisone is also linked to Idiopathic Uveitis, which is associated with Fluorometholone. These relationships imply a potential role of corticosteroids in the development of Uveitis, possibly through their anti-inflammatory effects. The presence of multiple pathways involving Fluorometholone and Uveitis suggests a broader mechanism by which Hydrocortisone may influence inflammatory processes in the eye. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of corticosteroids in modulating immune responses, potentially offering a rationale for their use in treating Uveitis.",
